Your custom annotation processor should analyze the codebase, identify all methods marked with `@Mandatory`, and then verify that these methods are implemented in all subclasses of the class containing the annotated method. If a subclass fails to implement a mandatory method, the processor should generate a compilation error to alert the developer.

Implement the logic for the custom annotation processor to enforce the presence of the `@Mandatory` annotation on methods and ensure their implementation in all subclasses.

